-- title:
--   Tail families of resolvent compositions
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $R_n$ be the resolvents of $T$.
--
--   1. **Tail family.** For $m\in\mathbb N$, the maps
--   $$
--   R_n\circ g,\qquad n\ge m,\ g\text{ generated}.
--   $$
--   Precomposing with a generated map keeps a map in the same tail.
--   2. **Ambient tail hull.** The convex hull of the tail family in the vector space of functions $K\to X$. Its members are genuine generated selfmaps, with approximate fixed point defect at most $1/m$ when $\operatorname{diam}K\le1$.
--   3. **Precomposition.** $f\mapsto f\circ g$ is linear on functions $K\to X$. Hence convex hulls are preserved, without any continuity or affinity of the nonlinear maps.
